Added `__traits(vtblSymbol)` and `__traits(getInterfaces)`

`__traits(vtblSymbol, C)` is the vtable of class `C`, of type `const(void*[])`.

`__traits(getInterfaces, C)` is the `Interface[]` array of class or interface
`C`, of type `const(Interface[])`. It is the array `TypeInfo_Class.interfaces`
refers to.

Like `__traits(initSymbol)`, these are slices of symbols whose contents are only
known at link time. Previously CTFE rejected any use of such a slice. It can now
be stored in a compile-time value, cast to another array type, and its `.length`
read. Reading its contents remains an error.

---
struct S { int a; long b; }

enum init = (() => __traits(initSymbol, S))();
static assert(init.length == S.sizeof);

enum first = (() => (cast(const(ubyte)[]) init)[0])();  // Error: cannot read the contents
---
